## Approach
The challenge provides a string of hexadecimal values 
that represent ASCII characters. Each hex value maps 
to a specific character — converting them all reveals 
the flag. Used CyberChef to automate the conversion 
instead of decoding each value manually.

## Solution

### Step 1 — Identify the Encoding
Recognized that each value starting with 0x is a 
hexadecimal number. In ASCII, hex values map directly 
to characters — for example 0x70 = 'p', 0x69 = 'i', 
0x63 = 'c', 0x6f = 'o' which spells the start of 
picoCTF.

### Step 2 — Use CyberChef to Decode
Opened CyberChef and used the From Charcode operation 
with base 16 to convert all hex values to their 
corresponding ASCII characters simultaneously.

Pasted the hex string into the input and the output 
revealed the full flag instantly.

